{"abstract":"Objective: To investigate how running, cycling, and sedentary cardiovascular stress impact biomarkers of cartilage turnover acutely in subjects with knee osteoarthritis (OA). Design: This was a sequential, cross-over, clinical study. Forty subjects with primary knee OA underwent moderate-to-high-intensity cycling, running, and adrenaline infusion on separate days. Blood was sampled before, during, and at 6-time points after intervention. On a control day, similar samples were taken. Biomarkers of type II collagen degradation (C2M, T2CM, Coll2-1, Coll2-1NO2), formation (PRO-C2), and aggrecan degradation (ARGS) were measured. Results: Mean age was 60.4 years, 40% were male, 45% had cumulated Kellgren-Lawrence (KL)-grade (Right + Left knee) of 2 to 3 and 55% had 4 to 6. Analyzing overall changes, area under the curve was significantly lower compared with resting values for ARGS and C2M after cycling and for ARGS after running. Considering individual time points, peak changes in biomarker levels showed reduction in C2M shortly following cycling (T20min = −12.3%, 95% confidence interval [CI]: −19.3% to −5.2%). PRO-C2 increased during cycling (T10min = 14.0%, 95% CI = 4.1% to 23.8%) and running (T20min = 16.5%, 95% CI = 4.3% to 28.6%). T2CM decreased after cycling (T50min = −19.9%, 95% CI = −29.2% to −10.6%), running (T50min = −22.8%, 95% CI = −32.1% to −13.5%), and infusion of adrenaline (peak, T50min = −9.8%, 95% CI = −20.0% to 0.4%). A latent increase was seen in Coll2-1 240 minutes after running (T260min = 21.7%, 95% CI = −1.6% to 45.1%). Conclusion: Exercise had an impact on cartilage markers, but it did not suggest any detrimental effect on cartilage. Changes following adrenaline infusion suggest a sympathomimetic influence on the serological composition of biomarkers.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Bjerre-Bastos, Jonathan J.","Sejersen, Casper","Nielsen, Henning Morris Bay","Boesen, Mikael","Secher, Niels H.","Distajo, Gregorio","Flood, Vincent","Henrotin, Yves","Uebelhoer, Melanie","Krustrup, Peter","Kitchen, Carl Christian","Thudium, Christian S.","Andersen, Jeppe R.","Bihlet, Asger R."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-814001"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bjerre-Bastos, Jonathan J."],"country":["Belgium","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Artialis Group","Artialis SA","Prosoft Clinical","University of Liege","University of Liège","VIVALIA","VIVALIA hospitals"],"keyword":["Adrenaline","Aged","Bicycling physiology","Biochemical markers","Biomarkers blood","Collagen Type II blood","Cross Over Studies","Epinephrine administration dosage","Exercise","Exercise Therapy methods","Exercise physiology","Female","Humans","Knee osteoarthritis","Male","Middle Aged","Osteoarthritis Knee physiopathology","Running physiology","Weight Bearing physiology","type II collagen"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NBIO","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-PR-NBIO","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the impact of weight bearing exercise non weight bearing exercise and cardiovascular stress on biochemical markers of cartilage turnover in patients with mild to moderate knee osteoarthritis a sequential cross over clinical study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/19476035241258170","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-814001","identifier":[{"id":"85195570228","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11569697","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"38853398","type":"pmid"}],"