{"abstract":"Insulin secretion is critical for glucose homeostasis, and increased levels of the precursor proinsulin relative to insulin indicate pancreatic islet beta-cell stress and insufficient insulin secretory capacity in the setting of insulin resistance. We conducted meta-analyses of genome-wide association results for fasting proinsulin from 16 European-ancestry studies in 45,861 individuals. We found 36 independent signals at 30 loci (p value < 5 × 10-8), which validated 12 previously reported loci for proinsulin and ten additional loci previously identified for another glycemic trait. Half of the alleles associated with higher proinsulin showed higher rather than lower effects on glucose levels, corresponding to different mechanisms. Proinsulin loci included genes that affect prohormone convertases, beta-cell dysfunction, vesicle trafficking, beta-cell transcriptional regulation, and lysosomes/autophagy processes. We colocalized 11 proinsulin signals with islet expression quantitative trait locus (eQTL) data, suggesting candidate genes, including ARSG, WIPI1, SLC7A14, and SIX3. The NKX6-3/ANK1 proinsulin signal colocalized with a T2D signal and an adipose ANK1 eQTL signal but not the islet NKX6-3 eQTL. Signals were enriched for islet enhancers, and we showed a plausible islet regulatory mechanism for the lead signal in the MADD locus. These results show how detailed genetic studies of an intermediate phenotype can elucidate mechanisms that may predispose one to disease.","author_count":71,"contributors":["Broadaway, K. Alaine","Yin, Xianyong","Williamson, Alice","Parsons, Victoria A.","Wilson, Emma P.","Moxley, Anne H.","Vadlamudi, Swarooparani","Varshney, Arushi","Jackson, Anne U.","Ahuja, Vasudha","Bornstein, Stefan R.","Corbin, Laura J.","Delgado, Graciela E.","Dwivedi, Om P.","Silva, Lilian Fernandes","Frayling, Timothy M.","Grallert, Harald","Gustafsson, Stefan","Hakaste, Liisa","Hammar, Ulf","Herder, Christian","Herrmann, Sandra","Højlund, Kurt","Hughes, David A.","Kleber, Marcus E.","Lindgren, Cecilia M.","Liu, Ching Ti","Luan, Jian'an","Malmberg, Anni","Moissl, Angela P.","Morris, Andrew P.","Perakakis, Nikolaos","Peters, Annette","Petrie, John R.","Roden, Michael","Schwarz, Peter E.H.","Sharma, Sapna","Silveira, Angela","Strawbridge, Rona J.","Tuomi, Tiinamaija","Wood, Andrew R.","Wu, Peitao","Zethelius, Björn","Baldassarre, Damiano","Eriksson, Johan G.","Fall, Tove","Florez, Jose C.","Fritsche, Andreas","Gigante, Bruna","Hamsten, Anders","Kajantie, Eero","Laakso, Markku","Lahti, Jari","Lawlor, Deborah A.","Lind, Lars","März, Winfried","Meigs, James B.","Sundström, Johan","Timpson, Nicholas J.","Wagner, Robert","Walker, Mark","Wareham, Nicholas J.","Watkins, Hugh","Barroso, Inês","O'Rahilly, Stephen","Grarup, Niels","Parker, Stephen Cj","Boehnke, Michael","Langenberg, Claudia","Wheeler, Eleanor","Mohlke, Karen L."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-043260"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Mohlke, Karen L."],"country":["Finland","Germany","Italy","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Boston University","Boston University School of Public Health","Dresden University of Technology","Eberhard Karls University of Tübingen","Friedrich Schiller University Jena","Friedrich Schiller University of Jena","German Center for Diabetes Research","Harvard University","Heidelberg University","Heinrich Heine University Düsseldorf","Helmholtz Zentrum München - German Research Center for Environmental Health","Institute of Human Genetics, Helmholtz Zentrum München","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska Institutet","MRC Epidemiology Unit","MRC Integrative Epidemiology Unit","Massachusetts General Hospital","Medizinische Fakultät Carl Gustav Carus","Newcastle University","Oulu University Hospital","University Hospital Dresden","University of Bristol","University of Cambridge","University of Eastern Finland","University of Exeter","University of Glasgow","University of Helsinki","University of Manchester","University of Michigan","University of Michigan, Ann Arbor","University of Milan","University of Newcastle","University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill","University of Oulu","University of Oxford","University of Tübingen","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Colocalization","Conditional","Enhancer","GWAS","Meta analysis","Proinsulin","SIGNAL","Type 2 diabetes","eQTL","fine mapping"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-STENO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"loci for insulin processing and secretion provide insight into type 000000000002 diabetes risk","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9943750/pdf/main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-043260","identifier":[{"id":"85147458360","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36693378","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9943750","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000951221200001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-6d193242-e117-4cc0-9e50-2cf8cd576a07","sdu-f248596a-5002-4b75-92a4-4e5eb92be299"],"keyword":["GWAS","colocalization","conditional","eQTL","enhancer","fine-mapping","meta-analysis","proinsulin","signal","type 2 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-20F4FE27F85882ADD7E1A2D1E4951C3A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9943750/pdf/main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of north carolina at chapel hil