tral","status":"p","title":"Genome Biology","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85144774123"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e7bba477-7adc-4e31-9042-ab6d9ff0d9a2","sdu-a82d0232-3b4d-4e7e-82db-1ed5ae20d9e7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Implicating genes, pleiotropy, and sexual dimorphism at blood lipid loci through multi-ancestry meta-analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-047005","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Positron emission tomography (PET) offers an incredible wealth of diverse research applications in vascular disease, providing a depth of molecular, functional, structural, and spatial information. Despite this, vascular PET imaging has not yet assumed the same clinical use as vascular ultrasound, CT, and MR imaging which provides information about late-onset, structural tissue changes. The current clinical utility of PET relies heavily on visual inspection and suboptimal parameters such as SUVmax; emerging applications have begun to harness the tool of whole-body PET to better understand the disease. Even still, without automation, this is a time-consuming and variable process. This review summarizes PET applications in vascular disorders, highlights emerging AI methods, and discusses the unlocked potential of AI in the clinical space.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Paravastu, Sriram S","Theng, Elizabeth H","Morris, Michael A","Grayson, Peter","Collins, Michael T","Maass-Moreno, Roberto","Piri, Reza","Gerke, Oke","Alavi, Abass","Høilund-Carlsen, Poul Flemming","Edenbrandt, Lars","Saboury, Babak"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-609852"],"filters":{"added":"2022-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Saboury, Babak"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","California University of Pennsylvania","National Institutes of Health","Sahlgrenska University Hospital","University of Maryland","University of Missouri-Kansas City"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Humans","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Positron Emission Tomography"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"artificial intelligence in vascular pet translational and clini