,"last":"Lambiase","name":"Lambiase, Pier D","rank":162,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nona","key":"sotoodehnianonapau","last":"Sotoodehnia","name":"Sotoodehnia, Nona","rank":163,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Borbala","key":"mifsudborbalapau","last":"Mifsud","name":"Mifsud, Borbala","rank":164,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"newtonchehchristopherpau","last":"Newton-Cheh","name":"Newton-Cheh, Christopher","rank":165,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Patricia B","key":"munroepatriciabpau","last":"Munroe","name":"Munroe, Patricia B","rank":166,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1101/2021.11.04.21265866","pages":"90","publisher":"Cold Spring Harbor Laboratory Press","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5a5487d2-76a1-400b-962e-72e76412ad5c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Genetic analyses of the QT interval and its components in over 250K individuals identifies new loci and pathways affecting ventricular depolarization and repolarization","type":"Preprint","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-076259","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Aims. We produce a clean and well-characterised catalogue of objects within 100 pc of the Sun from the Gaia Early Data Release 3. We characterise the catalogue through comparisons to the full data release, external catalogues, and simulations. We carry out a first analysis of the science that is possible with this sample to demonstrate its potential and best practices for its use. Methods. Theselection of objects within 100 pc from the full catalogue used selected training sets, machine-learning procedures, astrometric quantities, and solution quality indicators to determine a probability that the astrometric solution is reliable. The training set construction exploited the astrometric data, quality flags, and external photometry. For all candidates we calculated distance posterior probability densities using Bayesian procedures and mock catalogues to define priors. Any object with reliable astrometry and a non-zero probability of being within 100 pc is included in the catalogue. Results. We have produced a catalogue of 331 312 objects that we estimate contains at least 92% of stars of stellar type M9 within 100 pc of the Sun. We estimate that 9% of the stars in this catalogue probably lie outside 100 pc, but when the distance probability function is used, a correct treatment of this contamination is possible. We produced luminosity functions with a high signal-to-noise ratio for the main-sequence stars, giants, and white dwarfs. We examined in detail the Hyades cluster, the white dwarf population, and wide-binary systems and produced candidate lists for all three samples. We detected local manifestations of several streams, superclusters, and halo objects, in which we identified 12 members of Gaia Enceladus. We present the first direct parallaxes of five objects in multiple systems within 10 pc of the Sun. Conclusions. We provide the community with a large, well-characterised catalogue of objects in the solar neighbourhood. This is a primary benchmark for measuring and understanding fundamental parameters and descriptive functions in astronomy.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Smart, R. L.","Sarro, L. M.","Rybizki, J.","Reyle, C.","Robin, A. C.","Hambly, N. C.","Abbas, U.","Barstow, M. A.","de Bruijne, J. H. J.","Bucciarelli, B.","Carrasco, J. M.","Cooper, W. J.","Hodgkin, S. T.","Masana, E.","Michalik, D.","Sahlmann, J.","Sozzetti, A.","Brown, A. G. A.","Vallenari, A.","Prusti, T.","Babusiaux, C.","Biermann, M.","Creevey, O. L.","Evans, D. W.","Eyer, L.","Hutton, A.","Jansen, F.","Jordi, C.","Klioner, S. A.","Lammers, U.","Lindegren, L.","Luri, X.","Mignard, F.","Panem, C.","Pourbaix, D.","Randich, S.","Sartoretti, P.","Soubiran, C.","Walton, N. A.","Fabricius, C.","Smith, M.","Anderson, R. I.","Gerlach, E.","Hauser, M.","Lindstrøm, Hans Erik Peter","Morris, D.","Pagani, C.","Siebert, A.","Stephenson, C. A.","Zhao, H."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-481520"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["Gaia Collaboration"],"country":["Belgium","France","Germany","Italy","Netherlands","Spain","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Aurora Technol European Space Agcy ESA","CNES Ctr Spatial Toulouse","Dresden University of Technology","European Space Astron Ctr ESAC, European Space Agency, European Space Agcy ESA","European Space Res & Technol Ctr ESTEC, European Space Agency, European Space Agcy ESA","FRS FNRS, Fonds de la Recherche Scientifique - FNRS","Heidelberg University ","Istituto Nazionale di Astrofisica","Leiden University","Lund University","Max Planck Institute for Astrophysics","RHEA European Space Agcy ESA","UNED, Universidad Nacional de Educacion a Distancia (UNED), Dept Inteligencia Artificial","University of Barcelona","University of Burgundy","University of Cambridge","University of Côte d'Azur","University of Edinburgh","University of G