 Vasquez","rank":35,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"19","corresponding":null,"first":"Kenichi","key":"wadakenichipau","last":"Wada","name":"Wada, Kenichi","rank":36,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11 20","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Behnam","key":"zakeribehnampau","last":"Zakeri","locid":"732bf996-618a-467d-8f73-e560dcf66008","name":"Zakeri, Behnam","rank":37,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/1748-9326/abf964","issn":["17489326"],"issn_org":["17489318"],"issue":"5","journal":"Environmental Research Letters","paperid":"054046","publisher":"Institute of Physics","status":"p","title":"Environmental Research Letters","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85105919084"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a97085e0-66d8-4b7b-9647-40e8a639e7b4"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Integrated assessment model diagnostics : Key indicators and model evolution","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-099196","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Context. Gaia Early Data Release 3 (Gaia EDR3) provides accurate astrometry for about 1.6 million compact (QSO-like) extragalactic sources, 1.2 million of which have the best-quality five-parameter astrometric solutions. Aims. The proper motions of QSO-like sources are used to reveal a systematic pattern due to the acceleration of the solar systembarycentre with respect to the rest frame of the Universe. Apart from being an important scientific result by itself, the acceleration measured in this way is a good quality indicator of the Gaia astrometric solution. Methods. Theeffect of the acceleration was obtained as a part of the general expansion of the vector field of proper motions in vector spherical harmonics (VSH). Various versions of the VSH fit and various subsets of the sources were tried and compared to get the most consistent result and a realistic estimate of its uncertainty. Additional tests with the Gaia astrometric solution were used to get a better idea of the possible systematic errors in the estimate. Results. Our best estimate of the acceleration based on Gaia EDR3 is (2.32 +/- 0.16) x 10(-10) m s(-2) (or 7.33 +/- 0.51 km s(-1) Myr-1) towards alpha = 269.1 degrees +/- 5.4 degrees, delta = -31.6 degrees +/- 4.1 degrees, corresponding to a proper motion amplitude of 5.05 +/- 0.35 mu as yr(-1). This is in good agreement with the acceleration expected from current models of the Galactic gravitational potential. We expect that future Gaia data releases will provide estimates of the acceleration with uncertainties substantially below 0.1 mu as yr(-1).","author_count":49,"contributors":["Klioner, S. A.","Mignard, F.","Lindegren, L.","Bastian, U.","McMillan, P. J.","Hernandez, J.","Hobbs, D.","Ramos-Lerate, M.","Biermann, M.","Bombrun, A.","de Torres, A.","Gerlach, E.","Hilger, T.","Lammers, U.","Steidelmueller, H.","Stephenson, C. A.","Brown, A. G. A.","Vallenari, A.","Prusti, T.","de Bruijne, J. H. J.","Babusiaux, C.","Creevey, O. L.","Evans, D. W.","Eyer, L.","Hutton, A.","Jansen, F.","Jordi, C.","Luri, X.","Panem, C.","Pourbaix, D.","Randich, S.","Sartoretti, P.","Soubiran, C.","Walton, N. A.","Arenou, F.","Bailer-Jones, C. A. L.","Cropper, M.","Drimmel, R.","Katz, D.","Lattanzi, M. G.","Fabricius, C.","Smith, M.","Anderson, R. I.","Hauser, M.","Lindstrøm, Hans Erik Peter","Morris, D.","Pagani, C.","Siebert, A.","Zhao, H."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-429366"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["Gaia Collaboration"],"country":["Belgium","France","Germany","Italy","Netherlands","Spain","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Aurora Technol European Space Agcy ESA","CNES Ctr Spatial Toulouse","Dresden University of Technology","European Space Astron Ctr ESAC, European Space Agency, European Space Agcy ESA","European Space Res & Technol Ctr ESTEC, European Space Agency, European Space Agcy ESA","FRS FNRS, Fonds de la Recherche Scientifique - FNRS","HE Space Operat BV European Space Agcy ESA","Heidelberg University ","Istituto Nazionale di Astrofisica","Leiden University","Lund University","Max Planck Institute for Astrophysics","University College London","University of Barcelona","University of Cambridge","University of Côte d'Azur","University of Geneva","University of Padua","University of Turin","Université PSL","Université de Bordeaux","Vitrociset Belgium European Space Agcy ESA"],"keyword":["Astrometry","Distance","GALAXY","Kinematics","Large Magellanic Cloud","MASS","Methods data analysis","Perturbation","Proper motions","Reference systems","VIRGO CLUSTER","kinematics and dynamics","milky way"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gaia early data release