,"rank":439,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Carissa","key":"pinedafrankscarissapau","last":"Pineda-Franks","name":"Pineda-Franks, Carissa","rank":440,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wan","key":"asyrafwanpau","last":"Asyraf","name":"Asyraf, Wan","rank":441,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"no-firstname","key":"trungquochnguyennofirstnamepau","last":"Trung Quoch Nguyen","name":"Trung Quoch Nguyen, no-firstname","rank":442,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gabor","key":"tarkanyigaborpau","last":"Tarkanyi","name":"Tarkanyi, Gabor","rank":443,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Diogo","key":"haussendiogopau","last":"Haussen","name":"Haussen, Diogo","rank":445,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Oscar","key":"balagueraoscarpau","last":"Balaguera","name":"Balaguera, Oscar","rank":446,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Alejandro Rodriguez","key":"vasquezalejandrorodriguezpau","last":"Vasquez","name":"Vasquez, Alejandro Rodriguez","rank":447,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Raul","key":"nogueiraraulpau","last":"Nogueira","name":"Nogueira, Raul","rank":448,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00283878","1526632X"],"issn_org":["00283878"],"issue":"15 Supplement","journal":"Neurology","paperid":"1462","status":"p","title":"Neurology","volume":"96"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d1dd088b-350f-4ce1-baf0-5e3c72c08537"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Global impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on stroke care and intravenous thrombolysis","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-518849","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: The PRODIGE 7-trial investigated the additional value of Hyperthermic Intraperitoneal Chemotherapy (HIPEC) to cytoreductive surgery (CRS) for patients with colorectal peritoneal metastases (CPM). The results of PRODIGE 7 were presented at the 2018 ASCO meeting showing that 30 min oxaliplatin-based HIPEC did not improve overall survival. The current study investigated the impact of PRODIGE 7 on the worldwide practice of CRS and HIPEC. Materials and methods: CRS-HIPEC experts from 19 countries were invited through the Peritoneal Surface Oncology Group International (PSOGI) to complete an online survey concerning the current CRS-HIPEC practice in their hospital and country, and were asked to appraise the effect of PRODIGE 7. Results: The survey was completed by 18/19 experts. Although their personal opinions of CRS-HIPEC were barely influenced by PRODIGE 7, they reported a substantial impact on daily practice. This included a switch towards Mitomycin-C based HIPEC-regimens and prolongation of HIPEC perfusion time, a reduction in the number of referrals from non-HIPEC centers, a reduction in national consensus, the removal of HIPEC from national guidelines, and a reduced reimbursement rate. Conclusion: The PRODIGE 7 has had a major impact on the practice of CRS-HIPEC for CPM worldwide. HIPEC remains an attractive option with potential for control and eradication of disease and further studies into the optimal HIPEC-regimen are urgently needed. Meanwhile, given the complexity of the treatment of patients with CPM, and the proven benefits of optimal CRS, referral of patients with potentially resectable CPM to expert centers is recommended whilst the precise role of HIPEC is further evaluated.","author_count":24,"contributors":["van de Vlasakker, Vincent C.J.","Lurvink, Robin J.","Cashin, Peter H.","Ceelen, Wim","Deraco, Marcello","Goéré, Diane","González-Moreno, Santiago","Lehmann, Kuno","Li, Yan","Moran, Brendan","Morris, David L.","Piso, Pompiliu","Quadros, Claudio A.","Rau, Beate","Somashekhar, S. P.","Sommariva, Antonio","van der Speeten, Kurt","Spiliotis, John","Sugarbaker, Paul H.","Teo, Melissa C.C.","Verwaal, Victor Jilbert","Yonemura, Yutaka","Glehen, Olivier","de Hingh, Ignace H.J.T."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-602473"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["de Hingh, Ignace H.J.T."],"country":["Australia","Belgium","Brazil","China","France","Germany","Greece","India","Italy","Japan","Netherlands","Singapore","Spain","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Beijing Shijitan Hospital","Catharina Hospital","Charité - University Medicine Berlin","European Interbalkan Medical Center","Ghent University Hospital","Hampshire Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust","Hospital Barmherzige Brüder","Hospital São Rafael","Institut Gustave Roussy","Kishiwada Tokushukai Hospital","Lyon Sud Hospital Center","MD Anderson Cancer Center Madrid","Maastricht University","Manipal Comprehensive Cancer Center","National Cancer Centre Singapore","National Cancer Institute of Milan","The St George Hospital","University Hospital Zurich","University of Padova and Istituto Oncologico Veneto","Uppsala University","Washington Hospital Center","Ziekenhuis Oost-Limburg"],"keyword":["CRS HIPEC","HIPEC"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the impact of prodige 000000000007 on the current worldwide practice of crs hipec for colorectal peritoneal metastases a web based survey and 000000002021 statement by peritoneal surface oncology group international psogi","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"