{"abstract":"MASCARA-4 b is a hot Jupiter in a highly misaligned orbit around a rapidly rotating A3V star that was observed for 54 days by the Transiting Exoplanet Survey Satellite (TESS). We perform two analyses of MASCARA-4 b using a stellar gravity-darkened model. First, we measure MASCARA-4 b's misaligned orbital configuration by modeling its TESS photometric light curve. We take advantage of the asymmetry in MASCARA-4 b's transit due to its host star's gravity-darkened surface to measure MASCARA-4 b's true spin-orbit angle to be 104°. We also detect a ∼4σ secondary eclipse at 0.491 � 0.007 orbital phase, proving that the orbit is slightly eccentric. Second, we model MASCARA-4 b's insolation including gravity darkening and find that the planet's received X-ray and ultraviolet flux varies by 4% throughout its orbit. MASCARA-4 b's short-period, polar orbit suggests that the planet likely underwent dramatic orbital evolution to end up in its present-day configuration and that it receives a varying stellar irradiance that perpetually forces the planet out of thermal equilibrium. These findings make MASCARA-4 b an excellent target for follow-up characterization to better understand the orbital evolution and present-day environment of planets around high-mass stars.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Ahlers, John P.","Kruse, Ethan","Colón, Knicole D.","Dorval, Patrick","Talens, Geert Jan","Snellen, Ignas","Albrecht, Simon","Otten, Gilles","Ricker, George","Vanderspek, Roland","Latham, David","Seager, Sara","Winn, Joshua","Jenkins, Jon M.","Haworth, Kari","Cartwright, Scott","Morris, Robert","Rowden, Pam","Tenenbaum, Peter","Ting, Eric B."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-240040"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Ahlers, John P."],"country":["Canada","France","Netherlands","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["ASTRON","All Global Affiliations","Ames Research Center","French National Centre for Scientific Research (CNRS)","Leiden University","Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT)","NASA Goddard Space Flight Center","Open University Milton Keynes","Princeton University","SETI Institute","Smithsonian Institution","University of Montreal"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gravity darkening analysis of the misaligned hot jupiter mascara 000000000004 b","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1911.05025.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-240040","identifier":[{"id":"85081312799","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c1fdd5f1-ffc9-40b7-9eea-2f11d65634d8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AA264E6C40DB57E8CCA5D6F3B4C81C6F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1911.05025.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"nasa goddard space flight center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"NASA Goddard Space Flight Center","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"leiden university","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leiden University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"astron","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"ASTRON","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ca","key":"university of montreal","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Montreal","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":