{"abstract":"We employed Mendelian randomization (MR) to evaluate the causal relationship between leukocyte telomere length (LTL) and amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS) with summary statistics from genome-wide association studies (n = ~ 38,000 for LTL and ~ 81,000 for ALS in the European population; n = ~ 23,000 for LTL and ~ 4,100 for ALS in the Asian population). We further evaluated mediation roles of lipids in the pathway from LTL to ALS. The odds ratio per standard deviation decrease of LTL on ALS was 1.10 (95% CI 0.93–1.31, p = 0.274) in the European population and 0.75 (95% CI 0.53–1.07, p = 0.116) in the Asian population. This null association was also detected between LTL and frontotemporal dementia in the European population. However, we found that an indirect effect of LTL on ALS might be mediated by low density lipoprotein (LDL) or total cholesterol (TC) in the European population. These results were robust against extensive sensitivity analyses. Overall, our MR study did not support the direct causal association between LTL and the ALS risk in neither population, but provided suggestive evidence for the mediation role of LDL or TC on the influence of LTL and ALS in the European population.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Gao, Yixin","Wang, Ting","Yu, Xinghao","Ferrari, Raffaele","Hernandez, Dena G.","Nalls, Michael A.","Rohrer, Jonathan D.","Ramasamy, Adaikalavan","Kwok, John B.J.","Dobson-Stone, Carol","Brooks, William S.","Schofield, Peter R.","Halliday, Glenda M.","Hodges, John R.","Piguet, Olivier","Bartley, Lauren","Thompson, Elizabeth","Haan, Eric","Hernández, Isabel","Ruiz, Agustín","Boada, Mercè","Borroni, Barbara","Padovani, Alessandro","Cruchaga, Carlos","Cairns, Nigel J.","Benussi, Luisa","Binetti, Giuliano","Ghidoni, Roberta","Forloni, Gianluigi","Albani, Diego","Galimberti, Daniela","Fenoglio, Chiara","Serpente, Maria","Scarpini, Elio","Clarimón, Jordi","Lleó, Alberto","Blesa, Rafael","Waldö, Maria Landqvist","Nilsson, Karin","Nilsson, Christer","Mackenzie, Ian R.A.","Hsiung, Ging Yuek R.","Mann, David M.A.","Grafman, Jordan","Morris, Christopher M.","Attems, Johannes","Griffiths, Timothy D.","Rowe, James B.","Nielsen, Jørgen Erik","Hjermind, Lena Elisabeth"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-421207"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["International FTD-Genomics Consortium (IFGC)"],"country":["Australia","Canada","China","Italy","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Autonomous University of Barcelona","Guy's Hospital","IRCCS Centro San Giovanni di Dio Fatebenefratelli - Brescia","IRCCS Fondazione Ca'Granda – Ospedale Maggiore Policlinico - Milano","Institut Català de Neurociències Aplicades","Instituto de Salud Carlos III","Lund University","Mario Negri Institute for Pharmacological Research","National Institutes of Health","Neuroscience Research Australia","Northwestern University","Queen Square","University College London","University of Adelaide","University of Brescia","University of British Columbia","University of Cambridge","University of Manchester","University of Milan","University of New South Wales","University of Newcastle","University of Oxford","Washington University St. Louis","Women's and Children's Hospital Adelaide","Xuzhou Medical University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mendelian randomization implies no direct causal association between leukocyte telomere length and amyotrophic lateral sclerosis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-68848-9","versio