portal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.85-035607","year":"2019","yearsub":2020}
{"abstract":"Human genomics is undergoing a step change from being a predominantly research-driven activity to one driven through health care as many countries in Europe now have nascent precision medicine programmes. To maximize the value of the genomic data generated, these data will need to be shared between institutions and across countries. In recognition of this challenge, 21 European countries recently signed a declaration to transnationally share data on at least 1 million human genomes by 2022. In this Roadmap, we identify the challenges of data sharing across borders and demonstrate that European research infrastructures are well-positioned to support the rapid implementation of widespread genomic data access.","author_count":41,"contributors":["Saunders, Gary","Baudis, Michael","Becker, Regina","Beltran, Sergi","Béroud, Christophe","Birney, Ewan","Brooksbank, Cath","Brunak, Søren","Van den Bulcke, Marc","Drysdale, Rachel","Capella-Gutierrez, Salvador","Flicek, Paul","Florindi, Francesco","Goodhand, Peter","Gut, Ivo","Heringa, Jaap","Holub, Petr","Hooyberghs, Jef","Juty, Nick","Keane, Thomas M.","Korbel, Jan O.","Lappalainen, Ilkka","Leskosek, Brane","Matthijs, Gert","Mayrhofer, Michaela Th.","Metspalu, Andres","Navarro, Arcadi","Newhouse, Steven","Nyrönen, Tommi","Page, Angela","Persson, Bengt","Palotie, Aarno","Parkinson, Helen","Rambla, Jordi","Salgado, David","Steinfelder, Erik","Swertz, Morris A.","Valencia, Alfonso","Varma, Susheel","Blomberg, Niklas","Scollen, Serena"],"cuid":["S02-095.74-032892"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Scollen, Serena"],"country":["Austria","Belgium","Canada","Estonia","Finland","France","Germany","Luxembourg","Netherlands","Slovenia","Spain","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["Aix-Marseille Université","All Global Affiliations","BBMRI-ERIC","Barcelona Institute of Science and Technology","Barcelona Supercomputing Center-Centro Nacional de Supercomputación","Broad Institute of Harvard University and Massachusetts Institute of Technology","CSC - IT Center for Science Ltd.","European Molecular Biology Laboratory","Flemish Institute for Technological Research","KU Leuven","Ontario Institute for Cancer Research","Pompeu Fabra University","Science for Life Laboratory","Sciensano","University of Groningen","University of Helsinki","University of Ljubljana","University of Luxembourg","University of Manchester","University of Tartu","University of Zurich","Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam","Wellcome Genome Campus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"leveraging european infrastructures to access 000000000001 million human genomes by 000000002022","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/239934711/European_infrastructures_to_access_one_million_human_genomes_by_2022.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-095.74-032892","identifier":[{"id":"85071608186","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31455890","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7115898","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-0d753644-a898-40f8-9fc9-5b9da4e91aae","ku-f3d1d35b-334e-4bba-a9d0-872e37c61d87"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-AA25965C5CC5EA0EF7C4F1C2AD69201B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/250864728/European_infrastructures_to_access_one_million_human_genomes.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/239934711/Eu