{"abstract":"Hand grip strength is a widely used proxy of muscular fitness, a marker of frailty, and predictor of a range of morbidities and all-cause mortality. To investigate the genetic determinants of variation in grip strength, we perform a large-scale genetic discovery analysis in a combined sample of 195,180 individuals and identify 16 loci associated with grip strength (P<5 × 10-8) in combined analyses. A number of these loci contain genes implicated in structure and function of skeletal muscle fibres (ACTG1), neuronal maintenance and signal transduction (PEX14, TGFA, SYT1), or monogenic syndromes with involvement of psychomotor impairment (PEX14, LRPPRC and KANSL1). Mendelian randomization analyses are consistent with a causal effect of higher genetically predicted grip strength on lower fracture risk. In conclusion, our findings provide new biological insight into the mechanistic underpinnings of grip strength and the causal role of muscular strength in age-related morbidities and mortality.","author_count":51,"contributors":["Willems, Sara M.","Wright, Daniel J.","Day, Felix R.","Trajanoska, Katerina","Joshi, Peter K.","Morris, John A.","Matteini, Amy M.","Garton, Fleur C.","Grarup, Niels","Oskolkov, Nikolay","Thalamuthu, Anbupalam","Mangino, Massimo","Liu, Jun","Demirkan, Ayse","Lek, Monkol","Xu, Liwen","Wang, Guan","Oldmeadow, Christopher","Gaulton, Kyle J.","Lotta, Luca A.","Miyamoto-Mikami, Eri","Rivas, Manuel A.","White, Tom","Loh, Po Ru","Aadahl, Mette","Amin, Najaf","Attia, John R.","Austin, Krista","Benyamin, Beben","Brage, Søren","Cheng, Yu Ching","Ciȩszczyk, Paweł","Derave, Wim","Eriksson, Karl Fredrik","Eynon, Nir","Linneberg, Allan","Lucia, Alejandro","Massidda, Myosotis","Mitchell, Braxton D.","Miyachi, Motohiko","Murakami, Haruka","Padmanabhan, Sandosh","Pandey, Ashutosh","Papadimitriou, Ioannis","Rajpal, Deepak K.","Sale, Craig","Schnurr, Theresia M.","Sessa, Francesco","Shrine, Nick","Hansen, Torben"],"cuid":["S02-087.14-039948"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["GEFOS Any-Type of Fracture Consortium","et al."],"country":["Australia","Belgium","Canada","Italy","Japan","Netherlands","Poland","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Broad Institute","Erasmus University Medical Center Rotterdam","European University of Madrid","Gdańsk University of Physical Education and Sport","Ghent University","GlaxoSmithKline","Glenfield Hospital","Guy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundation Trust","Harvard Medical School","Harvard T.H. Chan School of Public Health","Hospital Universitario 12 de Octubre","Hunter Medical Research Institute","Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","Johns Hopkins University","King's College London","Leiden University","Lund University","Massachusetts General Hospital","McGill University","National Institute of Fitness and Sports Kanoya","National Institutes of Biomedical Innovation","Nottingham Trent University","San Diego Center of Excellence for Stress and Mental Health","Stanford University","The Royal Children's Hospital","The University of Edinburgh","The University of Queensland","University of Brighton","University of Cagliari","University of California","University of Cambridge","University of Foggia","University of Glasgow","University of Leicester","University of Maryland","University of New South Wales","University of Newcastle","Victoria University","​John Hunter Hospital"],"keyword":["Actins genetics","Adult","Aged","Cohort Studies","European Continental Ancestry Group genetics","Female","Genetic Loci","Genetics Population","Genome Wide Association Study","Hand Strength","Hand physiology","Humans","Male","Membrane Proteins genetics","Middle Aged","Neoplasm Proteins genetics","Nuclear Proteins genetics","Polymorphism Single Nucleotid