y":"odonovanmichaelcpau","last":"O'Donovan","name":"O'Donovan, Michael C","rank":315,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27792727"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pgen.1006343","issn":["15537390","15537404"],"issn_org":["15537390"],"issue":"10","journal":"PLoS Genetics","paperid":"e1006343","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLoS Genetics","title_org":"P L o S Genetics","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84994314495"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5e402a9b-771f-459f-84f5-6832d2865916","ku-7730682e-6ab1-409e-96eb-51c7fdf2d1fe"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"No Reliable Association between Runs of Homozygosity and Schizophrenia in a Well-Powered Replication Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.25-666264","year":"2016","yearsub":2017}
{"abstract":"Life sciences are yielding huge data sets that underpin scientific discoveries fundamental to improvement in human health, agriculture and the environment. In support of these discoveries, a plethora of databases and tools are deployed, in technically complex and diverse implementations, across a spectrum of scientific disciplines. The corpus of documentation of these resources is fragmented across the Web, with much redundancy, and has lacked a common standard of information. The outcome is that scientists must often struggle to find, understand, compare and use the best resources for the task at hand.Here we present a community-driven curation effort, supported by ELIXIR-the European infrastructure for biological information-that aspires to a comprehensive and consistent registry of information about bioinformatics resources. The sustainable upkeep of this Tools and Data Services Registry is assured by a curation effort driven by and tailored to local needs, and shared amongst a network of engaged partners.As of November 2015, the registry includes 1785 resources, with depositions from 126 individual registrations including 52 institutional providers and 74 individuals. With community support, the registry can become a standard for dissemination of information about bioinformatics resources: we welcome everyone to join us in this common endeavour. The registry is freely available at https://bio.tools.","author_count":69,"contributors":["Ison, Jon","Rapacki, Kristoffer","Ménager, Hervé","Kalaš, Matúš","Rydza, Emil","Chmura, Piotr","Anthon, Christian","Beard, Niall","Berka, Karel","Bolser, Dan","Booth, Tim","Bretaudeau, Anthony","Brezovsky, Jan","Casadio, Rita","Cesareni, Gianni","Coppens, Frederik","Cornell, Michael","Cuccuru, Gianmauro","Davidsen, Kristian","Vedova, Gianluca Della","Dogan, Tunca","Doppelt-Azeroual, Olivia","Emery, Laura","Gasteiger, Elisabeth","Gatter, Thomas","Goldberg, Tatyana","Grosjean, Marie","Grüning, Björn","Helmer-Citterich, Manuela","Ienasescu, Hans-Ioan","Ioannidis, Vassilios","Jespersen, Martin Closter","Jimenez, Rafael","Juty, Nick","Juvan, Peter","Koch, Maximilian","Laibe, Camille","Li, Jing-Woei","Licata, Luana","Mareuil, Fabien","Mičetić, Ivan","Friborg, Rune Møllegaard","Moretti, Sebastien","Morris, Chris","Möller, Steffen","Nenadic, Aleksandra","Peterson, Hedi","Profiti, Giuseppe","Rice, Peter","Romano, Paolo","Roncaglia, Paola","Saidi, Rabie","Schafferhans, Andrea","Schwämmle, Veit","Smith, Callum","Sperotto, Maria Maddalena","Stockinger, Heinz","Vařeková, Radka Svobodová","Tosatto, Silvio C. E.","de la Torre, Victor","Uva, Paolo","Via, Allegra","Yachdav, Guy","Zambelli, Federico","Vriend, Gert","Rost, Burkhard","Parkinson, Helen","Løngreen, Peter","Brunak, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-486431"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","Czechia","Estonia","France","Germany","Hong Kong","Italy","Netherlands","Norway","Slovenia","Spain","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bielefeld University","CRS4 Bioinformatics","Central European Institute of Technology","Chinese University of Hong Kong","Daresbury Laboratory","Department of Informatics, Bioinformatics-I12","Department of Plant Systems Biology, VIB","European Bioinformatics Institute (EMBL-EBI)","INRAE","IRCCS AOU San Martino IST","Imperial College London","Institut Francais de Bioinformatique","Institut Pasteur de Lille","Instruct, WTCHG","Masaryk University","NEBC Wallingford","National Bioinformatics Institute Unit","Palacký University Olomouc","Radboud University Nijmegen","Swiss Institute of Bioinformatics","The European Bioinformatics Institute (EMBL-EBI)","University of Bergen","University of Bologna","University of Freiburg","University of Ljubljana","University of Lübeck","University of Manchester","University of Milan","Universit