{"abstract":"After an initial meeting in 2013 that reviewed adherence to disease modifying therapy, the AD@MS group conducted a follow-up meeting in 2014 that examined adherence to behavioural interventions in MS (e.g. physical activity, diet, psychosocial interventions). Very few studies have studied adherence to behavioural interventions in MS. Outcomes beyond six months are lacking, as well as implementation work in the community. Psychological interventions need to overcome stigma and other barriers to facilitate initiation and maintenance of behaviour change. A focus group concentrated on physical activity and exercise as one major behavioural intervention domain in MS. The discussion revealed that patients are confronted with multiple challenges when attempting to regularly engage in physical activity. Highlighted needs for future research included an improved understanding of patients' and health experts' knowledge and attitudes towards physical activity as well as a need for longitudinal research that investigates exercise persistence.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Heesen, Christoph","Bruce, Jared","Gearing, Robert","Moss-Morris, Rona","Weinmann, John","Hamalainen, Paivi","Motl, Robert","Dalgas, Ulrik","Kos, Daphne","Visioli, Franceso","Feys, Peter","Solari, Alessandra","Finlayson, Marcia","Eliasson, Lina","Matthews, Vicki","Bogossian, Angeliki","Liethmann, Katrin","Köpke, Sascha","Bissell, Paul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-216291"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","Canada","Germany","Italy","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Columbia University","Guy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundation Trust","Hasselt University","KU Leuven","Queen's University Kingston","Royal Brompton and Harefield NHS Foundation Trust","University Medical Center Hamburg-Eppendorf","University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign","University of Lübeck","University of Milan","University of Missouri at Kansas City","University of Padova","University of Sheffield"],"keyword":["Adherence","Behavioural interventions","Exercise","Journal Article","Multiple sclerosis","Quality of Life","Rehabilitation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"adherence to behavioural interventions in multiple sclerosis follow up meeting report ad ms 000000000002","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/2055217315585333","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-216291","identifier":[{"id":"28607693","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5433389","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85047513168","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-98ac258b-c53f-461f-8770-5ae45ec5b19e"],"keyword":["Journal Article","adherence","behavioural interventions","exercise","multiple sclerosis","quality of life","rehabilitation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-50EC1CDC66C380664CBFB0B6357DC5AD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/2055217315585333","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university medical center hamburg eppendorf","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Medical Center Hamburg-Eppendorf","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of missouri at kansas city","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Missouri at Kansas City","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"columbia university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Columbia University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"guy s and st thomas nhs found