{"abstract":"We present the sixth catalog of Kepler candidate planets based on nearly four years of high precision photometry. This catalog builds on the legacy of previous catalogs released by the Kepler project and includes 1493 new Kepler Objects of Interest (KOIs) of which 554 are planet candidates, and 131 of these candidates have best-fit radii \\lt 1.5 {{R}\\oplus }. This brings the total number of KOIs and planet candidates to 7348 and 4175 respectively. We suspect that many of these new candidates at the low signal-to-noise ratio limit may be false alarms created by instrumental noise, and discuss our efforts to identify such objects. We re-evaluate all previously published KOIs with orbital periods of \\gt 50 days to provide a consistently vetted sample that can be used to improve planet occurrence rate calculations. We discuss the performance of our planet detection algorithms, and the consistency of our vetting products. The full catalog is publicly available at the NASA Exoplanet Archive.","author_count":46,"contributors":["Mullally, F.","Coughlin, Jeffrey L.","Thompson, Susan E.","Rowe, Jason","Burke, Christopher","Latham, David W.","Batalha, Natalie M.","Bryson, Stephen T.","Christiansen, Jessie","Henze, Christopher E.","Ofir, Aviv","Quarles, Billy","Shporer, Avi","Van Eylen, Vincent","Van Laerhoven, Christa","Shah, Yash","Wolfgang, Angie","Chaplin, W. J.","Xie, Ji-Wei","Akeson, Rachel","Barclay, Thomas","Borucki, William J.","Caldwell, Douglas A.","Campbell, Jennifer R.","Catanzarite, Joseph H.","Cochran, William D.","Duren, Riley M.","Girouard, Forrest R.","Haas, Michael R.","Howell, Steve B.","Huber, Daniel","Gautier, Thomas N., III","Jenkins, Jon M.","Li, Jie","Lissauer, Jack J.","Morris, Robert L.","Patil-Sabale, Anima","Quintana, Elisa V.","Ramirez, Solange","Silva Aguirre, Victor","Seader, Shawn","Smith, Jeffrey C.","Still, Martin","Tenenbaum, Peter","Twicken, Joseph D.","Zamudio, Khadeejah A."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-161782"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","China","Germany","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ames Research Center","California Institute of Technology","Nanjing University","Smithsonian Institution","University of Arizona","University of Birmingham","University of California","University of California at Santa Cruz","University of Göttingen","University of Sydney","University of Texas at Austin","Wyle Laboratories, Inc."],"keyword":["Catalogs","Eclipses","Planetary systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"planetary candidates observed by kepler vi planet sample from q000000000001 q000000000016 000000000047 months","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2015ApJS..217...31M","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-161782","identifier":[{"id":"84928538003","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-38dd33ad-3d8c-4434-88a9-bfeccc942a93"],"keyword":["catalogs","eclipses","planetary systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AEE74A929D9824F3A5243CF8414ED7BB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2015ApJS..217...31M","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"ames research center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Ames Research Center","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"smithsonian institution","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Smithso