,"first":"Andre G.","key":"uitterlindenandregpau","last":"Uitterlinden","name":"Uitterlinden, Andre G.","rank":46,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gonneke","key":"willemsengonnekepau","last":"Willemsen","name":"Willemsen, Gonneke","rank":47,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bruce H.","key":"wolffenbuttelbrucehpau","last":"Wolffenbuttel","name":"Wolffenbuttel, Bruce H.","rank":48,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Jun","key":"wangjunpau","last":"Wang","locid":"5dee6edc-2876-496f-a341-4a07933f9928","name":"Wang, Jun","rank":49,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Paul I. W.","key":"debakkerpauliwpau","last":"de Bakker","name":"de Bakker, Paul I. W.","rank":50,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gert-Jan","key":"vanommengertjanpau","last":"van Ommen","name":"van Ommen, Gert-Jan","rank":51,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Cornelia M.","key":"vanduijncorneliampau","last":"van Duijn","name":"van Duijn, Cornelia M.","rank":52,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23714750"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/ejhg.2013.118","issn":["10184813","14765438"],"issn_org":["10184813"],"journal":"European Journal of Human Genetics","pages":"221-227","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Human Genetics","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84892798985"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","bgi-europe"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-793eb80d-00f3-4181-b745-f0a6ff180792"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Genome of the Netherlands : design, and project goals","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-466015","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"We previously used a single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) in the CHRNA5-A3-B4 gene cluster associated with heaviness of smoking within smokers to confirm the causal effect of smoking in reducing body mass index (BMI) in a Mendelian randomisation analysis. While seeking to extend these findings in a larger sample we found that this SNP is associated with 0.74% lower body mass index (BMI) per minor allele in current smokers (95% CI -0.97 to -0.51, P = 2.00 × 10(-10)), but also unexpectedly found that it was associated with 0.35% higher BMI in never smokers (95% CI +0.18 to +0.52, P = 6.38 × 10(-5)). An interaction test confirmed that these estimates differed from each other (P = 4.95 × 10(-13)). This difference in effects suggests the variant influences BMI both via pathways unrelated to smoking, and via the weight-reducing effects of smoking. It would therefore be essentially undetectable in an unstratified genome-wide association study of BMI, given the opposite association with BMI in never and current smokers. This demonstrates that novel associations may be obscured by hidden population sub-structure. Stratification on well-characterized environmental factors known to impact on health outcomes may therefore reveal novel genetic associations.","author_count":65,"contributors":["Taylor, Amy E","Morris, Richard W","Fluharty, Meg E","Bjorngaard, Johan H","Åsvold, Bjørn Olav","Gabrielsen, Maiken E","Campbell, Archie","Marioni, Riccardo","Kumari, Meena","Hällfors, Jenni","Männistö, Satu","Marques-Vidal, Pedro","Kaakinen, Marika","Cavadino, Alana","Postmus, Iris","Husemoen, Lise Lotte N","Skaaby, Tea","Ahluwalia, Tarun Veer Singh","Treur, Jorien L","Willemsen, Gonneke","Dale, Caroline","Wannamethee, S Goya","Lahti, Jari","Palotie, Aarno","Räikkönen, Katri","Kisialiou, Aliaksei","McConnachie, Alex","Padmanabhan, Sandosh","Wong, Andrew","Dalgård, Christine","Paternoster, Lavinia","Ben-Shlomo, Yoav","Tyrrell, Jessica","Horwood, John","Fergusson, David M","Kennedy, Martin A","Frayling, Tim","Nohr, Ellen A","Christiansen, Lene","Ohm Kyvik, Kirsten","Kuh, Diana","Watt, Graham","Eriksson, Johan","Whincup, Peter H","Vink, Jacqueline M","Boomsma, Dorret I","Davey Smith, George","Lawlor, Debbie","Linneberg, Allan","Ford, Ian","Jukema, J Wouter","Power, Christine","Hyppönen, Elina","Jarvelin, Marjo-Riitta","Preisig, Martin","Borodulin, Katja","Kaprio, Jaakko","Kivimaki, Mika","Smith, Blair H","Hayward, Caroline","Romundstad, Pål R","Sørensen, Thorkild I A","Munafò, Marcus R","Sattar, Naveed"],"cuid":["S02-090.15-044155"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"stratification by smoking status reveals an association of chrna000000000005 a000000000003 b000000000004 genotype with body mass index in never smokers","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1004799","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-090.15-044155","identifier":[{"id":"84919663860","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25474695","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4256159","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-888dc193-57e0-4281-b8bc-10442b075571","sdu-763ad13f-4eab-4c96-8cdb-99f048fa6602"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-770B7A517E93FC44A2EF8CAC00B74642"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1004799","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"K