{"abstract":"Background There is little consensus on a standard approach to analysing bone scan images. The Bone Scan Index (BSI) is predictive of survival in patients with progressive prostate cancer (PCa), but the popularity of this metric is hampered by the tedium of the manual calculation. Objective Develop a fully automated method of quantifying the BSI and determining the clinical value of automated BSI measurements beyond conventional clinical and pathologic features. Design, setting, and participantsWe conditioned a computer-assisted diagnosis system identifying metastatic lesions on a bone scan to automatically compute BSI measurements. A training group of 795 bone scans was used in the conditioning process. Independent validation of the method used bone scans obtained ≤3 mo from diagnosis of 384 PCa cases in two large population-based cohorts. An experienced analyser (blinded to case identity, prior BSI, and outcome) scored the BSI measurements twice. We measured prediction of outcome using pretreatment Gleason score, clinical stage, and prostate-specific antigen with models that also incorporated either manual or automated BSI measurements. MeasurementsThe agreement between methods was evaluated using Pearson's correlation coefficient. Discrimination between prognostic models was assessed using the concordance index (C-index). Results and limitations Manual and automated BSI measurements were strongly correlated (ρ=0.80), correlated more closely (ρ=0.93) when excluding cases with BSI scores ≥10 (1.8%), and were independently associated with PCa death (p<0.0001 for each) when added to the prediction model. Predictive accuracy of the base model (C-index: 0.768; 95% confidence interval [CI], 0.702–0.837) increased to 0.794 (95% CI, 0.727–0.860) by adding manual BSI scoring, and increased to 0.825 (95% CI, 0.754–0.881) by adding automated BSI scoring to the base model. ConclusionsAutomated BSI scoring, with its 100% reproducibility, reduces turnaround time, eliminates operator-dependent subjectivity, and provides important clinical information comparable to that of manual BSI scoring. We developed and evaluated the first unbiased, fully automated software system to systematically calculate skeletal tumour burden in patients with metastatic cancer in the bone, simplifying a valuable but cumbersome technology with shortcomings that had prevented its widespread clinical use.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Ulmert, David","Kaboteh, Reza","Fox, Josef J.","Savage, Caroline","Evans, Michael J.","Lilja, Hans","Abrahamsson, Per-Anders","Björk, Thomas","Gerdtsson, Axel","Bjartell, Anders","Gjertsson, Peter","Höglund, Peter","Lomsky, Milan","Ohlsson, Mattias","Richter, Jens","Sadik, May","Morris, Michael J.","Scher, Howard I.","Sjöstrand, Karl","Yu, Alice","Suurküla, Madis","Edenbrandt, Lars","Larson, Steven M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-364914"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","EXINI Diagnostics AB","Lund University","Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center","University of Gothenburg"],"keyword":["Automated detection","Automated quantification","Bone metastases","Bone scan index","Computer assisted diagnosis","Image analysis","Radionuclide Imaging","Risk prediction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a novel automated platform for quantifying the extent of skeletal tumour involvement in prostate cancer patients using the bone scan index","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eururo.2012.01.037","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-364914","identifier":[{"id":"84861602779","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ca01b661-53fa-4cb0-a3c9-639f8f353ea1"],"keyword":["Automated detection","Automated quantification","Bone Scan Index","Bone metastases","Computer assisted diagnosis","Image analysis","Radionuclide imaging","Risk prediction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-EDD829B3B90C06637408148F1C014336"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eururo.2012.01.037","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"university of gothenburg","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Gothenburg","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"memorial sloan kettering cancer center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"exini diagnostics ab","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"EXINI Diagnostics AB","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Informatics and Mathematical Modeling","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Informatics and Mathematical Modeling, DTU Data Analysis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"ulmertpau","last":"Ulmert","name":"Ulmert, David","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Reza","key":"kabotehpau","last":"Kaboteh","name":"Kaboteh, Reza","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Josef J.","key":"foxpau","last":"Fox","name":"Fox, Josef J.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Caroline","key":"savagepau","last":"Savage","name":"Savage, Caroline","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael J.","key":"evanspau","last":"Evans","name":"Evans, Michael J.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans","key":"liljapau","last":"Lilja","name":"Lilja, Hans","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per-Anders","key":"abrahamssonpau","last":"Abrahamsson","name":"Abrahamsson, Per-Anders","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"björkpau","last":"Björk","name":"Björk, Thomas","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Axel","key":"gerdtssonpau","last":"Gerdtsson","name":"Gerdtsson, Axel","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"bjartellpau","last":"Bjartell","name":"Bjartell, Anders","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"gjertssonpau","last":"Gjertsson","name":"Gjertsson, Peter","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"höglundpau","last":"Höglund","name":"Höglund, Peter","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Milan","key":"lomskypau","last":"Lomsky","name":"Lomsky, Milan","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mattias","key":"ohlssonpau","last":"Ohlsson","name":"Ohlsson, Mattias","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"richterpau","last":"Richter","name":"Richter, Jens","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"May","key":"sadikpau","last":"Sadik","name":"Sadik, May","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael J.","key":"morrispau","last":"Morris","name":"Morris, Michael J.","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Howard I.","key":"scherpau","last":"Scher","name":"Scher, Howard I.","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Karl","key":"sjöstrandpau","last":"Sjöstrand","locid":"3edc13db-4ec6-434a-84bc-564decd4ace0","name":"Sjöstrand, Karl","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Alice","key":"yupau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Alice","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Madis","key":"suurkülapau","last":"Suurküla","name":"Suurküla, Madis","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"edenbrandtpau","last":"Edenbrandt","name":"Edenbrandt, Lars","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Steven M.","key":"larsonpau","last":"Larson","name":"Larson, Steven M.","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.eururo.2012.01.037","issn":["03022838","1421993X"],"issn_org":["03022838"],"issue":"1","journal":"European Urology","pages":"78-84","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"European Urology","volume":"62"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84861602779"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ca01b661-53fa-4cb0-a3c9-639f8f353ea1"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A Novel Automated Platform for Quantifying the Extent of Skeletal Tumour Involvement in Prostate Cancer Patients Using the Bone Scan Index","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-364914","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"To extend understanding of the genetic architecture and molecular basis of type 2 diabetes (T2D), we conducted a meta-analysis of genetic variants on the Metabochip, including 34,840 cases and 114,981 controls, overwhelmingly of European descent. We identified ten previously unreported T2D susceptibility loci, including two showing sex-differentiated association. Genome-wide analyses of these data are consistent with a long tail of additional common variant loci explaining much of the variation in susceptibility to T2D. Exploration of the enlarged set of susceptibility loci implicates several processes, including CREBBP-related transcription, adipocytokine signaling and cell cycle regulation, in diabetes pathogenesis.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Morris, Andrew P","Voight, Benjamin F","Teslovich, Tanya M","Ferreira, Teresa","Segrè, Ayellet V","Steinthorsdottir, Valgerdur","Strawbridge, Rona J","Khan, Abid Hassan","Grallert, Harald","Mahajan, Anubha","Prokopenko, Inga","Kang, Hyun Min","Dina, Christian","Esko, Tonu","Fraser, Ross M","Kanoni, Stavroula","Kumar, Ashish","Lagou, Vasiliki","Langenberg, Claudia","Luan, Jian'an","Lindgren, Cecilia M","Müller-Nurasyid, Martina","Pechlivanis, Sonali","Rayner, N William","Scott, Laura J","Wiltshire, Steven","Yengo, Loic","Kinnunen, Leena","Rossin, Elizabeth J","Raychaudhuri, Soumya","Johnson, Andrew D","Dimas, Antigone S","Loos, Ruth J F","Vedantam, Sailaja","Chen, Han","Florez, Jose C","Fox, Caroline","Liu, Ching-Ti","Rybin, Denis","Couper, David J","Kao, Wen Hong L","Li, Man","Cornelis, Marilyn C","Kraft, Peter","Sun, Qi","van Dam, Rob M","Stringham, Heather M","Jonsson, Anna","Lind, Lars","Njølstad, Inger"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-528481"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium"],"keyword":["Case Control Studies","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2","Female","GENES","Genetic Predisposition to Dis