-026876","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Cigarette smoking is associated with lower body mass index (BMI), and a commonly cited reason for unwillingness to quit smoking is a concern about weight gain. Common variation in the CHRNA5-CHRNA3-CHRNB4 gene region (chromosome 15q25) is robustly associated with smoking quantity in smokers, but its association with BMI is unknown. We hypothesized that genotype would accurately reflect smoking exposure and that, if smoking were causally related to weight, it would be associated with BMI in smokers, but not in never smokers.","author_count":28,"contributors":["Freathy, Rachel M","Kazeem, Gbenga R","Morris, Richard W","Johnson, Paul C D","Paternoster, Lavinia","Ebrahim, Shah","Hattersley, Andrew T","Hill, Anita","Hingorani, Aroon D","Holst, Claus","Jefferis, Barbara J","Kring, Sofia I I","Mooser, Vincent","Padmanabhan, Sandosh","Preisig, Martin","Ring, Susan M","Sattar, Naveed","Upton, Mark N","Vollenweider, Peter","Waeber, Gerard","Sørensen, Thorkild I A","Frayling, Timothy M","Watt, Graham","Lawlor, Debbie A","Whincup, Peter H","Tozzi, Federica","Davey Smith, George","Munafò, Marcus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-511265"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic variation at chrna000000000005 chrna000000000003 chrnb000000000004 interacts with smoking status to influence body mass index","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ije/dyr077","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-511265","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3235017","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"81455135676","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21593077","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c572e8dc-e831-449f-9106-6de67a450289"],"lang":"English","level":"S